# Phase 2 CLI acceptance — edition identity/primary/license surface (D-07)

`QAI_DATA_DIR` points the real `qai` binary at a fresh temp database (set by the
harness); the synthetic identity fixture declares a non-null upstream identity,
`is_primary: true`, and a concrete license, so `edition show` can report all
three on the human line and in `--json`.

```console
$ qai db migrate
migrations applied; schema version 21

```

```console
$ qai quran import ../../fixtures/quran/test-edition-identity/manifest.json
imported test-edition-identity@0.1.0 to Staged
note: synthetic test data — non-canonical (ADR-0101 fallback)

```

```console
$ qai quran activate test-edition-identity@0.1.0 --yes
activated test-edition-identity@0.1.0 (generation 1)

```

The human line carries the declared upstream identity, the Q-ai edition id, the
primary marker, and the declared license status. It stays free of volatile ids.

```console
$ qai quran edition show test-edition-identity@0.1.0
test-edition-identity@0.1.0 — Synthetic identity/primary fixture (non-canonical)
status: active
upstream: synthetic-identity-upstream
qai-id: qai:synthetic-identity
primary: true
license: verified

```

```console
